======================================================================================
ROUTE G: the COLLAPSE LEMMA for the signed relation-lattice kernel K(n)
======================================================================================

[0] EXACT inner coefficient c(z,|S|) = sum_{T sup S}(-1)^|T|(1-|T|/7)^z
    (z = # zero-coords of n;  S = sector-image of the assignment)
      z \ |S|: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
      z=0: ['0', '0', '0', '0', '0', '0', '1']
      z=1: ['0', '0', '0', '0', '0', '-1/7', '1/7']
      z=2: ['0', '0', '0', '0', '2/49', '-3/49', '1/49']
      z=3: ['0', '0', '0', '-6/343', '12/343', '-1/49', '1/343']
      z=4: ['0', '0', '24/2401', '-60/2401', '50/2401', '-15/2401', '1/2401']
      z=5: ['0', '-120/16807', '360/16807', '-390/16807', '180/16807', '-31/16807', '1/16807']

    SHARP VANISHING (exact):  c(z,s)=0  <=>  s < 6 - z.
    c(z,s)=0 iff s<6-z  VERIFIED for all 0<=z,s<=6:  True
    => apex-prime invariant:  (#zeros z) + (min sector-image 6-z) = 6 = 7-1.

[1] CROSS-CHECK  Kk_collapse == Kk_direct  (numeric, several relation vectors)
